/**
 * Web-native representation layer: mobject -> SVG element.
 *
 * This module owns the *only* geometry the web-native backend keeps: whatever
 * the browser itself stores inside the generated DOM.  Nothing here caches
 * beziers, sampled points or per-frame interpolation state; a mobject is turned
 * into `d`/attribute values, written once into an element and then left alone
 * until its geometry, colour or style actually changes.
 *
 * Two rules drive the design:
 *
 *  - **Vectorized mobjects become `<path>`/`<circle>`/`<line>`/...** with the
 *    world-space `d` computed from `VMobject.points` (the camera transform is
 *    applied by the SVG viewBox, not per element).
 *  - **Text and math are DOM content**, produced by KaTeX / the browser text
 *    engine, and carried on the mobject as a {@link NativeTextPayload}.  They
 *    are never parsed back into beziers.
 *
 * The writer is incremental: {@link AttributeWriter} remembers what it last
 * wrote on an element and skips identical values, so a frame that only moves a
 * `Dot` costs one `transform` write instead of a full style recalculation.
 */
